 "notes": [
  "steady24h dispatches are dominated by N=1 batches (p50 = 1 image/batch) with a heavy tail to the cap (p99 = 64). Both vLLM tables are dense over N=1..64 and every dispatched N is an exact table key in all three cells, so no interpolation and no extrapolation is exercised (dispatch_n_not_in_table is empty everywhere).",
  "steady24h__fc and steady24h__re return the SAME retimed p99 to full float precision (direct 741.987, per-N 745.833) even though their stored simulator p99 differ (681.117 vs 684.999), their dispatches differ (39906 vs 39899 batches) and 1686 of the 88260 per-request delays differ. It is a genuine order-statistic coincidence at the p99 index, not an input mix-up: the immediate neighbours of the p99 order statistic, the p99.9 and the max all differ between the two arms.",
  "The static-C8 arm is the only steady24h cell whose retimed p99 sits far below the others; the reactive and forecast arms are provisioned more thinly in this window, which is why their p99 encoder delay is higher under every service representation."
 ]
